(To Sherlock Holmes she is always _the_ woman. I have seldom heard him) Tj
T*
(mention her under any other name. In his eyes she eclipses and) Tj
T*
(predominates the whole of her sex. It was not that he felt any emotion) Tj
T*
(akin to love for Irene Adler. All emotions, and that one particularly,) Tj
T*
(were abhorrent to his cold, precise but admirably balanced mind. He) Tj
T*
(was, I take it, the most perfect reasoning and observing machine that) Tj
T*
(the world has seen, but as a lover he would have placed himself in a) Tj
T*
(false position. He never spoke of the softer passions, save with a gibe) Tj
T*
(and a sneer. They were admirable things for the observer-excellent for) Tj
T*
(drawing the veil from men's motives and actions. But for the trained) Tj
T*
(reasoner to admit such intrusions into his own delicate and finely) Tj
T*
(adjusted temperament was to introduce a distracting factor which might) Tj
T*
(throw a doubt upon all his mental results. Grit in a sensitive) Tj
T*
(instrument, or a crack in one of his own high-power lenses, would not) Tj
T*
(be more disturbing than a strong emotion in a nature such as his. And) Tj
